# sources and targets

Insert here: @target[foo]

@begin(source){target=foo}
This is **sourced** content with a [link](https://example.com).
@end(source)

A target before its source, alone on its line:

@target[later]

And the emoji form: 🎯later in a sentence.

@begin(source){target=later}
The *later* source, with a list:

- one
- two
@end(source)

@begin(source){target=nowhere}
A source with no target is gone.
@end(source)

@begin(source){target=foo}
A second source for foo is gone too.
@end(source)

@target[missing] has no source.

@begin(source){target=self}
Itself: @target[self] (nothing).
@end(source)

@target[self]
